---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const pageTitle = "Privacy Policy";
const description = "Privacy Policy for AuthenticNerd.com";
const lastUpdated = "February 24, 2026";
---

<BaseLayout pageTitle={pageTitle} description={description} ogType="website">
  <div class="leading-relaxed text-inherit">
    <section class="my-8">
      <h1 class="text-navy mb-2 text-4xl leading-tight font-bold italic dark:text-white">
        The "Authentic Nerd" Privacy Policy
      </h1>
      <p class="mb-4 text-sm opacity-70">Last Updated: {lastUpdated}</p>
      <p class="border-terracotta bg-navy/5 border-l-4 py-2 pl-4 text-lg italic dark:bg-white/5">
        "I value your privacy as much as I value my own system's uptime."
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="my-8">
      <h2 class="text-navy mb-4 text-2xl font-bold dark:text-white">Zero Client-Side Tracking</h2>
      <p class="mb-4">
        I recently made the architectural decision to remove all client-side analytics from this site. There is no
        Google Analytics, no AWS Real User Monitoring, and no marketing pixels.
      </p>
      <ul class="mb-4 ml-2 list-inside list-disc space-y-2">
        <li>
          <strong>No Cookies:</strong> This system does not set any tracking cookies on your device.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>No Cross-Site Tracking:</strong> I do not track your behavior across the internet. There are no "Like" buttons
          or third-party ad networks here.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Read in Peace:</strong> Whether you use a standard browser or a heavily locked-down setup with strict tracking
          protection, the site will function exactly the same.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="my-8">
      <h2 class="text-navy mb-4 text-2xl font-bold dark:text-white">Infrastructure & Security Logs</h2>
      <p class="mb-4">
        While the frontend is completely free of trackers, the underlying infrastructure (AWS CloudFront and Web
        Application Firewall) automatically generates standard edge access logs to keep the system secure and online.
      </p>
      <ul class="mb-4 ml-2 list-inside list-disc space-y-2">
        <li>
          <strong>Edge Routing:</strong> When you request a page, AWS temporarily processes your IP address to route you to
          the closest edge node for sub-second load times.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>System Security:</strong> Automated bots and malicious requests are blocked at the edge. Standard request
          data (IP, User-Agent, URI) is logged in a secure, private bucket strictly for security audits and debugging routing
          failures.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Data Lifecycle:</strong> I do not stockpile this data. All infrastructure logs are governed by a strict
          lifecycle policy and are permanently destroyed after 90 days.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="border-navy/10 my-8 border-t pt-8 dark:border-white/10">
      <h2 class="text-navy mb-4 text-xl font-bold dark:text-white">Contact</h2>
      <p>
        If you have questions about this policy or the system architecture, feel free to reach out via
        <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/jerometerry" target="_blank" class="text-terracotta hover:underline"
          >LinkedIn
        </a> or check the source code on
        <a href="https://github.com/jerometerry/authenticnerd" target="_blank" class="text-terracotta hover:underline"
          >GitHub
        </a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
